excerpt: 'A fundamental requirement for the understanding and verifiability of scientific results is the disclosure of data, methods and the scientific instruments used. In computer science, this relates primarily to technical artefacts, which conferences now require to be made available as part of the peer-review process. This paper investigates whether these artefacts are still available even years after their initial publication.'
